{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8c2f5d3b8941526fc57209109c4a0627cfaf9fd4ce1ad9848c66ceaf4a9d9987","digest":{"component_or_area":".github/workflows CI gate steps","key_entities":[".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py","scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py","raw-git-write gate","wall-clock-assert gate"],"problem_keywords":["CI workflow","gate step","pre-gate changes","tree-workflow skew","missing script","Gerrit verify"],"propositions":["New gate steps in _build-and-test.yml run scripts unconditionally, causing hard failures on pre-gate changes whose tree predates the script commit.","Gerrit CI loads workflow definition from target branch but checks out the change's tree, creating a divergence window where a script exists in the workflow but not in the checked-out tree.","Gate steps must guard script execution with existence checks to skip with an explanatory message when the script is absent, allowing pre-gate changes to pass without hard failure.","The idiom (if-present check with skip message) and rationale must be documented inline in the workflow so future gate authors copy the guard pattern."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787351093864570001,"uuid":"29cd19bc-b25a-4dae-916b-ebfac0f9e966"}